{
  "chapter": "first-agent/one-call",
  "tier": "build",
  "notes": [
    "The first piece of Atlas: a router. One model call per ticket, structured output, and",
    "control flow that belongs entirely to your code.",
    "The model's classification is scripted here, because what this exercise builds is the",
    "part around the call — the routing table and the scoreboard.",
    "Category correctness and routing correctness are different measurements. Two categories",
    "that share a queue mean a mislabelled ticket can still reach the right place.",
    "answerable_from_ticket_alone is a self-report. It is scored against reality and it is",
    "never used to decide anything.",
    "A ticket counts as resolved by this one call only if it was genuinely answerable from",
    "its own text and the category was right. That number is the ceiling."
  ],
